tion.The scent of medical formalin, wet cedar crate shavings, and Victor Haldane's signature Latakia Turkish pipe tobacco rising up the stairwell.Using her father's WARD C brass key, Clara unlocks the tin-clad fire door into a whitewashed brick morgue vault lined with four stainless-steel refrigeration lockers running at $4^\circ\text{C}$.In the center of the floor sits a freshly pried shipping crate stenciled with the crest of the Portland Custom House Wharf (proving the refrigeration crates from the 2023 Portland wharf fire were moved here).On a stainless-steel autopsy table lies her father's original 1998 Vance Maritime & Cargo black leather manifest binder, open to a bonded passenger-and-specimen transfer log from a vessel that supposedly sank off Block Island 26 years ago—with the final line item, written in her father's square draftsman's print, circled twice in fresh red grease pencil.Before she can read the circled name, the lights snap off and someone (Victor Haldane or his operative with the steel toe-tap) slams and bolts the exterior iron bulkhead doors, trapping Clara inside the $4^\circ\text{C}$ morgue vault as the tide turns.3. KEY QUESTIONS & PAYOFFS SET UP FOR BOOK 3 (THE QUARANTINE MANIFEST)When you write Book 3, these are the four central mysteries already planted for the reader:What (or Who) Is Inside the Six Refrigerated Crates in Ward C?In 1998, Clara's father certified six refrigerated containment crates offloaded from a vessel that "sank" off Block Island, logged on a passenger-and-specimen transfer log. In 2023, the Commercial Street wharf fire in Portland was staged to cover the replacement/movement of those cold-storage compressors and crates back to Barrow Island.Whose Name Is Circled in Red Grease Pencil on the 1998 Manifest?Written in Clara's father's hand on the final line of the 1998 passenger-and-specimen log—is it someone connected to Clara and Maya's family (e.g., their mother, a test subject, or the true founder behind the Mercer-H